{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"feedable-clannish-mite","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Mirror inventory finding F5 (reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md), HIGH, ALREADY DRIFTED.\nDistinct from the MCP-tool-vs-facade parity gate (ticket 8ce5-b870-601d-4715): this is\nmodels-vs-schemas.\n\nsrc/rebar/_mcp_models.py:1-24 declares itself a pydantic-only leaf with no rebar.* edges, so every\nenum must be hand-copied:\n- :61-68 PinStatus (6) vs llm/plan_review/pin_health.py:21\n- :54 TargetPinStatus (4) vs pin_health.py:29 (third copy as dict keys at :193)\n- :122 FileImpactScope vs types.py:22\n- :284-295, :298, :336 vs schemas/bridge_{run,status,access_check}.schema.json\n\nTwo gaps in schemas/check_mcp_models.py:\n1. missing_declarations (:51-57) is a PROPERTY-NAME set difference; it never reads `enum`.\n2. MODEL_SCHEMAS (:22-34) covers 11 of 34 *Out models. Running the gate predicate over the\n   unregistered ones: TicketStateOut missing 23 properties, NextBatchOut 11, GateResultOut 5,\n   CreateResultOut 1. Both PlanReviewHealth*Out (carrying the pin_status copies) absent entirely.\n\nThis is the published MCP wire contract.\n\nProposed fix: add-parity-check — compare enum values, and derive/assert MODEL_SCHEMAS completeness\ninstead of hand-listing it.","id":"62eb-5e6f-512a-420d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP output models re-type canonical enums and the drift gate is enum-blind (mirror F5)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788317556152213001,"uuid":"35fe7266-cad6-48e8-98dd-4c056d54090d"}